SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson 
 Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must b
 e checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Time
  is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minute
 s before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair a
 nd Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHAN
 GE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal a
 re the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1
 xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP 
 for Cherubs: Angels - Cherubs — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless T
 ights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\; Makeup:
  Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provide
 s): Gold Halo headpiece\; Prop (BA provides): Harp\nLight Stage Makeup I
 nstruction Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown
  eye shadow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark
  Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush 
 on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed o
 ut in the stage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Co
 lor may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Car
 e Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to
  prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arka
 nsas in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matte
 r how significant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the fl
 oor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sit
 ting on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, me
 nd\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply st
 age make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from s
 mudging make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the 
 use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any
  garment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume f
 ood or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  
 Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the th
 eater\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs
  following their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned ba
 gs\n•  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ 
 wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks
  or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
