  / HAIR / MAKEUP for Cherubs: Angels - Cherubs — Costume (you provide)
 : Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Balle
 t Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Access
 ories (BA provides): Gold Halo headpiece\; Prop (BA provides): Harp\nLig
 ht Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skintone\n
 •  Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease with an eye shadow 
 brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lash
 es.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer does
 n’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red lips
 tick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet 
 shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with car
 e while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly
  notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of d
 iscovery\, no matter how significant\n•  Never throw costumes or ac
 cessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• 
  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not a
 ttempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n
 •  Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great 
 care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n•
   Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n
 •  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do n
 ot handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the except
 ion of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressin
 g rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secur
 e head pieces and wigs following their use\n•  Return all headpiece
 s to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any and all updates 
 to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, p
 aints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
